"comparison": "Both disclosures address Level 3 valuations requiring significant unobservable inputs and the judgment involved. Citi notes that if quoted prices are unavailable, fair value relies on internally developed models using market-based parameters (c_2024_7_P669_S002). Goldman Sachs similarly states that Level 3 instruments require one or more significant inputs that are not observable (gs_2024_7_P018_S001) and that estimating their fair value requires judgments to be made (gs_2024_7_P018_S006). Furthermore, both mention valuation adjustments; Citi mentions using market-based or independently sourced parameters (c_2024_7_P669_S002), while Goldman Sachs explicitly lists adjustments for factors such as counterparty credit quality, liquidity, and bid/offer spreads (gs_2024_7_P017_S002).",
