"comparison": "Both Citi and JPMorgan emphasize the role of judgment in fair value estimation, particularly for Level 3 instruments using internally developed models. Citi states that when quoted prices are not available, fair value is based on internally developed valuation models (c_2024_7_P669_S002). JPMorgan aligns with this by stating that for instruments classified within Level 3 using internally developed models and significant unobservable inputs, the judgments used to estimate fair value are more significant than those for Levels 1 and 2 (jpm_2024_7_P792_S004). JPMorgan further details that management must determine the appropriate valuation model and assess empirical data to derive inputs (jpm_2024_7_P793_S001, jpm_2024_7_P793_S002), mirroring Citi's reliance on internally developed models using market parameters.",
